in the marketable securities when adjusted for inflation, showing remarkable stability in the government's securities during this period.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_118e69421a7e42c6a67d52f0","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# CPI-U (not seasonally adjusted) values for 1949 from Bureau of Labor Statistics\n# November 1949: 171.6\n# December 1949: 171.3\n\ncpi_nov_1949 = 171.6\ncpi_dec_1949 = 171.3\n\n# Total marketable securities outstanding subject to statutory debt limitation\n# From Treasury Bulletin data (in millions of dollars)\nnov_1949_marketable = 155205  # November 1949\ndec_1949_marketable = 154962  # December 1949\n\n# Adjust to constant December 1949 dollars\n# Formula: Value_adjusted = Value_current * (CPI_target / CPI_source)\n# For November 1949 value in constant December 1949 dollars:\nnov_adjusted = nov_1949_marketable * (cpi_dec_1949 / cpi_nov_1949)\ndec_adjusted = dec_1949_marketable  # Already in December 1949 dollars\n\nprint(f\"November 1949 value adjusted to constant Dec 1949 dollars: ${nov_adjusted:,.2f} million\")\nprint(f\"December 1949 value in constant Dec 1949 dollars: ${dec_adjusted:,.2f} million\")\n\n# Calculate absolute difference\nabs_difference = abs(dec_adjusted - nov_adjusted)\nprint(f\"\\nAbsolute difference (rounded to nearest whole number): ${round(abs_difference):,} million\")\n\n# Calculate absolute percentage difference\n# Percentage difference = |(new - old)| / old * 100\nabs_pct_difference = abs(dec_adjusted - nov_adjusted) / nov_adjusted * 100\nprint(f\"Absolute percentage difference: {abs_pct_difference:.6f}%\")\nprint(f\"Absolute percentage difference (rounded to 3 decimal places): {round(abs_pct_difference, 3)}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
